{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested","id":1106465,"title":"Newbies campaign - creative input requested","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-22T03:43:19-07:00","id":1106465,"title":"Newbies campaign - creative input requested","content":"Hey all, <br /> Just been approved so glad to be able to get in here and start posting. In the research for my campaign I was reading past threads on here all the time :-)<br /> I've got a bit of experience with storytelling, and fell in love with Mage about 16 years ago, but this is my first time running a game of it (apart from a half-baked shambles 8 years back). <br /> I think I've cracked the formula of how to avoid the usual pitfalls of storytelling mage - two of my players are brand new to wod and haven't really got their teeth into rpg's yet, and the third is a keen roleplayer without a powergaming bone in his body. They've all started as sleepers, just awakened, and they will learn about the universe and metaphysics in-character so as to avoid overcomplication or zany exploitation. <br /> <br /> I'm running a fairly simple 3-part intro story to get them awakened and aware of the major issues of the world, before letting them loose on the world to learn, explore, and ruin personal relationships. <br /> <br /> Part 1, last night, had them as mere sleepers trapped on a tram in the middle of a fight between a marauder and the technocracy. They each awoke simultaneously to survive a missile strike that incinerated their fellow passengers, but the paradox from proximity to the marauder knocked them all out. <br /> Part 2, next week, will have them as &quot;guests&quot; of a woman-in-black at a private hospital, being interrogated, tortured and/or recruited depending on their behaviour. This will give them a chance to learn about the technocracy in their own words and learn more about what is going on. They might also be able to try out some minor intentional magic if they can make sense of how to do that. <br /> Part 3 has them being rescued by local traditionalists, and receiving another recruitment offer from a different perspective, having a lot of paranoia instilled in them, but then having the chance to make up their own minds as to what to do with themselves.<br /> <br /> Thereafter, plots will be based on their actions, choices and backgrounds. <br /> What I'd like to do is post up on here and trade ideas to get the creative juices flowing. Hopefully some of you might enjoy such an exercise as well :-)<br /> <br /> For starters, I'm planning out the next session, reading the guide to the technocracy, and would like to make both the WiB and her methods memorable, and her philosophy somewhat sympathetic but a bit off as well. <br /> No William Wallace freedom speeches from the players as they're outsiders to the ascension war, and no evil rants from her either. <br /> <br /> So given that premise, does anyone have any ideas about her, her methods, or her philosophy? I like the Battlestar Galactica shades of grey character types. (I'm also watching Voyager just now so am strongly tempted to base her on Janeway!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13587,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","user":"Eyrelliah","date":". 06-22-2017, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T03:52:24-07:00","id":1106466,"title":"","content":"Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T03:55:00-07:00","id":1106469,"title":"","content":"What I read gives me the strong impression that one of the major themes is \u201cthe Choice\u201c.<br /> <br /> Keep up with that. Show your players how their choices matter in good and bad terms.<br /> <br /> Do you have plans if some PC's choose Technocracy and some Traditions?<br /> Or have they to make the choice as a group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:03:38-07:00","id":1106489,"title":"","content":"Have the capture by the technocracy be a rescue at the same time. Maybe the fire is closing in as they pass out and the last thing they see is a team of MiB with fire extinguishers... Dousing the flames. Will somewhat offset the torture thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:07:39-07:00","id":1106492,"title":"","content":"Thanks - I will indeed. One of the core themes in mage is how actions have consequences, and I want the game to be very much about the players' agency. <br /> <br /> Regarding a split between Traditions and technocracy, I've weighted things a bit by giving them a choice of loose paradigm during cc. And I plan to have them out on their own for a bit to work it out amongst themselves as a group. But I hadn't actually thought of that! <br /> I think that if there's a split I'll have both sides of the Ascension War be quite distant and hands-off, like the allies background rather than constant, up close npc's. That would let the characters exist in a &quot;no man's land&quot; between the organisations. They'll be orphans, begging for scraps from their masters' tables, and be exploited periodically. Should allow them to function as a group without being torn apart. <br /> <br /> The joy of less advance planning :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:11:02-07:00","id":1106494,"title":"","content":"@enginseer - I like that! <br /> I had them black out at the end of the session, but I can have things start out real nice with the hospital staff treating them properly and the &quot;emergency services&quot; who saved them stopping by to check in and make sure they're OK. Really humanise them with some teasing amongst the rescuers as they relate the story of their rescue. <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:16:48-07:00","id":1106561,"title":"","content":"Really interested in seeing how this goes. Keep it up, Eyrelliah. Can you tell us more about the characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:50:21-07:00","id":1106624,"title":"","content":"Sure - all I asked them for initially was name, age, education, income and family friends, and got them to pick one of the following to indicate a possible future paradigm:<br /> &quot;The world is a strange place. What do you believe?:<br /> There are secret laws that most people don\u2019t understand that allow strange things to happen<br /> Science can allow very strange things to happen - a lot of pseudoscience isn\u2019t as pseudo as they\u2019d have you believe<br /> Karma and fate govern reality more than physical laws<br /> The most important thing in reality is life, and the power of life can change reality<br /> Knowing your mind and yourself can change the world<br /> There is something great hidden behind the mask of religions<br /> This world is a shadow of the true world, where the true forms of all things can be found and bargained with<br /> Reality is probabilities and math. Sometimes you can tweak the odds.<br /> Reality has a pulse, if you\u2019re in touch with your senses you can feel the truth behind everything.<br /> Other - you tell me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Since then they've put some stats and skills down, which I haven't fully analysed yet but fit with what they have given me. <br /> <br /> Laura is an early-20's waitress in a vegan diner, chose the verbena option, Irish heritage and from North Manchester; her parents are working class and still together, she lives at home with them and her wee sister of whom she is fiercely protective. Loves the music scene. <br /> Sarah is an early 20's psychology graduate from Whitby who works as a healthcare assistant, got a straitlaced brother who is also in Manchester and encourages her to settle down with someone asap-chose the akashic option;<br /> John is in his late 30's and works as a coroner, chose the euthanatos option (and despite being the most experienced roleplayer and knowing mage already, hasn't given me much to be going on with background-wise!) <br /> <br /> They got some dots based on the awakening-effect that saved them from a technocracy missile strike, which were time, forces, and entropy respectively, then assigned the rest at all but still need to discover all of them in-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:21:20-07:00","id":1106629,"title":"","content":"&quot;Verbena&quot;, &quot;Akashic&quot;, and &quot;Euthanatos&quot;? Sounds like you're already pushing them towards the Traditions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:41:43-07:00","id":1106635,"title":"","content":"Well you may have noticed there's nine paradigm suggestions up there ;-) <br /> But in all honesty I don't know the technocracy that well, at least not as well as I know the Traditions, and I sold the premise to the newbies as &quot;magic in the modern world. You choose how it works for your character&quot;. <br /> I thought giving paradigm suggestions would help them find a tradition mentor, but hey if they go technocracy I'll run with it! Or if they don't like the tradition they have the best chance with, they can try and find another mentor. Or just stay orphan :-)<br /> <br /> There are tensions already that will make good roleplay possibilities - vegan verbena? Akashic whose player doesn't fancy martial arts? And a euthanatos whose first awakened act was to doom an innocent to die in his place? <br /> <br /> Yes, plenty of fun to be had. Together with seekings, developing a paradigm and learning rotes, balancing the real world with moral responsibility, learning about paradox the hard way... Jings I'm excited!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T23:15:48-07:00","id":1106899,"title":"","content":"So, this NWO agent - I'm planning on having her be the only Enlightened agent in the private hospital, but that could change based on the actions of the players - if they manage to break some stuff, someone else might be there to do repairs - although they could be an Extraordinary Citizen. <br /> I'm planning that the players will be &quot;in traction&quot;, or rather, restrained &quot;for their own good&quot;, and picture these restraints to look like those round frames put around a really messed up broken limb - the kind where they drill into the bone? <br /> Initially they will be horizontal, as if they're in a bed, but it turns out they're combination hospital bed, restraint, and exo-suit. It gives them something to struggle with and am easy way for the Agent to control them. <br /> I also thought I'd keep in mind that the rest of the Agent's team was killed or badly hurt by the marauder, so she's feeling pretty devastated. Keeping the job up but that'll be under the surface. <br /> There will be noticeable armed guards outside the door of the room as well. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a sequence of escalation for this second session. So, wake up, all seems good, look here's the people who saved you! Oh there's just a few formalities to deal with. Then the mind games begin. Accusations, intimidation, what were you doing, etc. <br /> I'm thinking of having the Agent take them away one at a time (remote controlled exo-suits of course) and cross-examine them, which means me doing that with the players. Is that a good format for a single session? <br /> She's going to do an intelligence community style interrogation, based on what I've seen on tv. <br /> <br /> The overall goal is to recruit, or just break the players. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone got suggestions on details of tactics or style the NWO would use? Without resorting straight to brainwashing? <br /> <br /> The end of the session will come with an offer of help from the Traditions, so I just want to make a satisfying session that builds tension before that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T06:39:26-07:00","id":1106994,"title":"","content":"Responsibility. Guilt. The players have the power to prevent things like that train accident, if only they would join the Technocracy. Seems like that might get to the proto-Euthanatos in particular given his sacrifice of someone else to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T07:21:15-07:00","id":1107006,"title":"","content":"The NWO agent using the Marauder as an example of Magic out of control could be a good counterargument to the Tradition's desire to make their arts public and accepted. She could even try to convince them that all mages become marauders eventually, this is the consequence of prolonged exposure to a universe governed by ones own personal belief system rather than trying to adhere to a more structured approach. The Technocracy keep people safe in many ways, not just by fighting away the boogy man. Their structure means marauders are much less common than they used to be.<br /> <br /> Just as some general advice. Don't skip out on the mundane, think about how their adventures affect their sleeper lives, their friends and family, their work, their home life. Part of what makes the technocracy so powerful is how much influence they have on the stuff we take for granted. Does your player want to advance with their career? The technocracy can help with that. Are police taking a sudden interest in your life? The Technocratic Union can make the investigation &quot;go away&quot;. Want your name on the lips of every academic in Harvard? A bit of media attention to bring your Kickstarter campaign the money it deserves? Or maybe just a little extra cash to help you through the week? The Union provides. Helping the Union can give you a plethora of enticing benefits, as well as access to a whole slew of tech. Advanced security? Genius pills? The fastest internet speeds this side of the Digital Web? All of it can be yours.<br /> <br /> Granted, this style of material bargaining is much more the Syndicate's game, the NWO are no strangers to creating mutual agreements for a few diplomatic endeavours.<br /> <br /> After all, why brainwash when they already think you're the good guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:58:34-07:00","id":1107079,"title":"","content":"Buildng on what Saikou says, if the characters have family and ties to the normal world, working within the Technocracy can be their best choice if they want to be protected from things that go bump in tha night and not live on the run. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T00:18:22-07:00","id":1107245,"title":"","content":"Thanks folks! <br /> So I'm thinking it'd be best to divide the session into 3 or 4 acts. More on that below. <br /> <br /> In terms of defining the character and her motivations, Agent Roe was the coordinator for the amalgam that got steamrollered by the marauder, and used excessive firepower that killed the civilians in the tram to die. <br /> She's gone a little rogue in taking the pc's off for interrogation and possible conversion, as she's trying to salvage her career from this disaster. She has support from unenlightened agents but is &quot;off grid&quot; from major technocracy support - thus meaning the players can escape later without bringing a full pogrom down on themselves (that's not the kind of game they want). <br /> <br /> So, acts:<br /> 1. Back to normality - experiencing what you'd expect as survivors of a disaster, waking up in hospital. <br /> 2. Interrogation - &quot;just a matter of protocol&quot;, gradually amping up the paranoia. Cross-questioning, being asked questions they can't answer, etc. <br /> 3. Persuasion - as you've described above. Together with threats. <br /> <br /> Then the end of the session is when they're given a reprieve to think the offer over, and are approached by a cleaner with the offer of escape...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T12:13:49-07:00","id":1107397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1107006#post1107006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as some general advice. Don't skip out on the mundane, think about how their adventures affect their sleeper lives, their friends and family, their work, their home life. Part of what makes the technocracy so powerful is how much influence they have on the stuff we take for granted. Does your player want to advance with their career? The technocracy can help with that. Are police taking a sudden interest in your life? The Technocratic Union can make the investigation &amp;quot;go away&amp;quot;. Want your name on the lips of every academic in Harvard? A bit of media attention to bring your Kickstarter campaign the money it deserves? Or maybe just a little extra cash to help you through the week? The Union provides. Helping the Union can give you a plethora of enticing benefits, as well as access to a whole slew of tech. Advanced security? Genius pills? The fastest internet speeds this side of the Digital Web? All of it can be yours.<br /> <br /> Granted, this style of material bargaining is much more the Syndicate's game, the NWO are no strangers to creating mutual agreements for a few diplomatic endeavours.<br /> <br /> After all, why brainwash when they already think you're the good guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>On this specifically, very yes. I want the campaign to be 1/3rd external supernatural, 2/3rds mundane/personal supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:15:49-07:00","id":1108385,"title":"","content":"So does anyone have any last-minute suggestions for the personality of agent roe? Or have any examples of really well-written NWO agents they've encountered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T21:36:23-07:00","id":1108618,"title":"","content":"not sure if this is too late, but my suggestion would be to make her a convert herself. Perhaps she was at one point a traditionist and then was converted over to the Technocracy after being captured/betraying her chantry/left with no other option. Might make some interesting side stories if she ends up becoming a recurring character. <br /> <br /> FYI I love what you have written about this so far, please keep up the posts. I would love to hear more about it. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2779-darkeye4876","name":"Darkeye4876","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T21:56:47-07:00","id":1108623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkeye4876</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1108618#post1108618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not sure if this is too late, but my suggestion would be to make her a convert herself. Perhaps she was at one point a traditionist and then was converted over to the Technocracy after being captured/betraying her chantry/left with no other option. Might make some interesting side stories if she ends up becoming a recurring character. <br /> <br /> FYI I love what you have written about this so far, please keep up the posts. I would love to hear more about it. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not too late! I'm running the game every Wednesday night (GMT) at present, so that is excellent, much appreciated! I'm currently speeding through the NWO convention book and have just reached the section about converts :-) <br /> <br /> So, I've already got a plan for an akashic, virtual adept, ecstatic and a verbena Npc in Manchester. I would like to make Roe a recurring character, so am not sure whether to have Roe be converted from one of those Traditions (for Drama) or other ones (to give breadth). I'd welcome anyone's tuppence on the subject!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T00:05:44-07:00","id":1108646,"title":"","content":"Personally I would go for an akashic convert. But either of the three would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T01:50:58-07:00","id":1108664,"title":"","content":"Akashic eh? Well that does make for an interesting story as the vanguard of the tradition &quot;rescue party&quot; will be an Akashic li hai in her 50's. Could have been her pupil! <br /> How would you portray an Akashic NWO convert? What would be their philosophy, motivation, worldview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T03:50:07-07:00","id":1108685,"title":"","content":"Well, Akashics are rather notorious for their strict discipline, adherence to the rules of Do, and their insistence on eastern style hands off teaching. This can be a very frustrating environment for a new Mage to struggle with. It's all of the rigour and expectation of the Hermetics with none of the support of one to one tuition.<br /> <br /> This is especially the case if an initiate is interested in things their mentor disapproves of, such as tech of western Psychology . Their master would only tell them that they are failing, and their disregard of the old ways is the reason for their failure. Being told time and again that something you rely on makes you a disappointment can be enough reason to pull out the middle finger and walk away.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they find the NWO method of psychology has much more in common with the Akashic principles of mental betterment than their masters lead on. Perhaps they even see that the Akashics methods can be explained with NWO psychological studies, and it's in fact the Tehcnocracy who is more open to these techniques and other traditional techniques being incorporated into normal practice while the Akashicks are being stuck up about how Do is the only real path to ascension.<br /> <br /> The reality may be that the NWO only try to describe the Akashics techniques scientifically as a method to demystify it, and make it seem more &quot;oh, I guess anyone can do it&quot;. Effectively making the masses trivialise the work and mental stamina that the Akashics practice into a series of self help book style Eastern Medicine stuff.<br /> <br /> How aware of this your NWO lady is is up to you. Perhaps they are still stary eyed on how amazing the technocracy is, perhaps they actively want to bring the Akashics down a peg because she knows they aren't as special as they think hey are, and their arrogance is iritating her.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could be more personal than this. Perhaps this agent was from Myanmar, and she saw first hand how brutal the Bhudist monks are in that region, bhudist monks backed by Akashic values. Perhaps a more fictional thing happened where she, her family, or other things she cares about where betrayed by these so called &quot;enlightened few&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's a lot less insidious, maybe she tried some psychology, ended up liking it, and the technocracy is much more tolerant of religious views than Tradition propaganda would have you believe, at least as far as she knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:27:57-07:00","id":1108789,"title":"","content":"Grand, I can run with that. Now just got to get my head and the rest of the details together for tonight! <br /> Thanks all for your help so far :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13587,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","user":"Eyrelliah","date":".  Predictive text 06-28-2017, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:36:29-07:00","id":1108947,"title":"","content":"Well! <br /> Session 2 complete. We didn't have the full 2 hours tonight as we had to finish everyone's character sheets off, but it worked really well - a lot of my prep wasn't necessary as the characters ended up in the right mood without much prompting. <br /> They awoke in the private hospital ward, recognising that it wasn't NHS, and Sarah became paranoid straight away when the first nurse she spoke to refused to talk to her about the incident and ran off to get someone more senior when she mentioned wildebeest. <br /> I decided that John had been buried under the entire tram-load of corpses and had a near death experience (that's what you get for choosing a euthanatos-orphan awakening) but the others were fine, although they were all strapped into these strange frames. Roe comes in after a brief conversation between the players, summons the friendly emergency workers who are all so pleased that the characters are OK, then dismisses them abruptly. She doesn't identify herself beyond being in &quot;national security&quot; and refers most of their concerns to &quot;my superiors&quot; or &quot;the security blackout&quot;, then takes them each aside to an interview room to ask their version of events. They each give a different one - Laura flat-out denial that she remembers anything, sarah outrage, especially when she starts thinking she's a terror suspect, and john a morphine-addled sweating paranoia as he admits seeing some strange things - but the best bit is what the other two, left in the room, are saying to each other. <br /> Paranoia mounts, and they're left alone by Roe while she &quot;reports to her superiors&quot;. That's when they start talking about how they should have coordinated their stories, shortly before discovering that there's cctv and they were probably being listened to the whole time. <br /> John scouts the loo in a fit of paranoia and discovers that the mirror is false. He tries to hang a towel on it subtly and fails. <br /> <br /> They discover the windows are barred. <br /> They try and fail to talk to the armed guards outside the door. <br /> They discover that their exo-suit bed-frames are extremely advanced and can be remote controlled. <br /> They decide by committee that they hate Agent Roe. <br /> They're ignored from late morning to night. <br /> They stew. <br /> <br /> Then, at 20 past midnight, they're woken by a &quot;psst&quot;, and find a middle-aged afro-carribean cleaning lady in the room, mopping the floor. <br /> <br /> She asks, &quot;would you like to get out?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13587,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","user":"Eyrelliah","date":".  Improvements 06-28-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:42:02-07:00","id":1109284,"title":"","content":"Two hour sessions? Wow, that's short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T10:35:06-07:00","id":1109309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1109284#post1109284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two hour sessions? Wow, that's short.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we all work full time and Laura's player is in a long-distance relationship so we can't do daytime or weekends. So instead we meet frequently for short sessions - weekly if possible. 7-9 is what we aim for, although last time was delayed by half an hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T13:44:18-07:00","id":1109380,"title":"","content":"So, I've got a bit of time to work on my next creative bit, since we're not meeting for another fortnight.<br /> Given the timescale per-session, I want to put in 2-3 tasks that the players can do to aid their escape. more on those below.<br /> <br /> The setup is that they've been found by my Akashic NPC, Etta, who is a middle-aged li-hai with arcane 4. She makes herself effectively invisible by simply being a middle-aged female cleaner - which works far too well in the UK these days.<br /> She's managed to get into them by putting the sleeper technocracy guards under a mind effect. and since she was anticipating trouble, has mopped the corridors with a little matter and forces to make the floor essentially frictionless. And she was the mentor of the traitor Agent Roe.<br /> She'll probably also need to put the players in a brief trance-state to remind them that they have powers as well, a little guided meditation to make them 'notice' their rank 1 spheres, and then get them to see if they can figure out a way to use the higher spheres.<br /> <br /> In order for the players to get away scot free, they'll need to:<br /> locate and trash all the data that Roe has on them;<br /> possibly help Etta to incapacitate Roe long enough to do a mind wipe on her; and<br /> set up an escape route.<br /> <br /> For the escape route I'm not sure whether to go with correspondence or spirit. Correspondence will require my VA NPC, who will also be needed to cover their tracks and erase the data that Roe has on them. I'm thinking that she'll reassign all of the suspicion and magickal traces to the dead from The Incident, so that anyone trying to recreate what Roe learned will be led to the dead from the tram. So correspondence would be cool. The VA won't be able to get in until Roe's defences are down however, as she's a Technocracy Coordinator with good Correspondence wards on the building at present. Thus Etta's old-school infiltration.<br /> I'm also tempted by a dreamspeaker Wonder I read about in forged in dragon's fire however - a carpet that lets you get through the gauntlet without being subject to the avatar storm, by stepping through it. <br /> In either case, the players would need to get a message to those persons for Etta. That could be by bribing a nearby spirit to go get the person with the carpet, or some kind of electronic gibberish message to the VA. That would allow the 'escape route' NPC to get to them, and then get them out.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any cool thoughts for how that correspondence/spirit shenanigans could be handled? I'm thinking a combination of cool setpieces with tasks the players need to achieve.<br /> <br /> When they get out, they'll briefly visit the nearest Chantry before being sent to 'lay low' at Glastonbury Festival. That will free things up for some downtimes telling the story of their experiences there with their new powers, and maybe meeting potential mentors among the crowds or at the Node.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T18:01:45-07:00","id":1109511,"title":"","content":"For my money, I like Correspondence. It's a little more manageable for most paradigms to wrap their heads around. You could do it Matrix style effectively Making a Correspondence 4/Life 5/Force 3 rote were they need to find a hardline to be &quot;Transported&quot; to the safe zone, but in order to safely escape they need to remove some security system scanning the lines for any interference, no sense trying to escape only to have your bits scattered into a million pieces in the information super highway lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2779-darkeye4876","user":"Darkeye4876","date":". 06-29-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2779-darkeye4876","name":"Darkeye4876","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:05:52-07:00","id":1109537,"title":"","content":"The only advice I would give is cast a wide net.<br /> <br /> Personally, I try to avoid having specific requirements that the players can either succeed or fail at. Rather, I prefer to have the characters and setting exist, and see how the players approach it, and react from there.<br /> <br /> This is probably not the best thing to do if you need the players to be in a certain place by the end of the second hour of real time, but it's still doable if the scale of possibility is influenced somewhat.<br /> <br /> Rather than choose between Corr and Spirit escape routes, why not allow the players to decide? Have things open to them, let them weigh up the risks vs rewards, and allow the players to surprise you with their own hair-brained scheme. Pay careful attention to what and how they decide to do it, and always allow for some degree of success if it seems plausible enough. Usually it's much more fun to let the players get away with something, and then let their mistakes unfold as consequences later down the line, than to just hit them with a brick wall with the message &quot;Wrong! Try again&quot; etched on the side.<br /> <br /> Some of the best games I've run involved my players frantically searching the book for ideas on how to exploit their spheres for whatever obstacle I placed in front of them. More often than not, the best and most effective solutions (or at least the most entertaining or spectacular) are ones that never crossed my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T03:05:45-07:00","id":1109675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1109537#post1109537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the best games I've run involved my players frantically searching the book for ideas on how to exploit their spheres for whatever obstacle I placed in front of them. More often than not, the best and most effective solutions (or at least the most entertaining or spectacular) are ones that never crossed my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree wholeheartedly with this sentiment when running a normal rpg with experienced players, in this case I don't think it would work. Since only 1 of my 3 players knows the rules at all, and the other two haven't read the rulebook (and probably won't for months while they finish their doctorates), I'm still at the stage of dripfeeding rules to them to get stuff done each session. <br /> So I would like to get them more creative, but giving them tasks to complete will give them a feel for *how* to get creative. Think of it like going trike-training wheels-bike :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:34:50-07:00","id":1109692,"title":"","content":"Posted the last one before it was finished - so, I want them to get to the stage where they can perform such acts, but I was thinking in this case that by giving them specific acts to achieve in order to be rescued by npc's, they can start expanding their agency. <br /> If they don't manage them, Etta can manage quite a lot on her own, but I want them to figure out for themselves what t they can do to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:45:44-07:00","id":1109697,"title":"","content":"Posted the last one before it was finished - so, I want them to get to the stage where they can perform such acts, but I was thinking in this case that by giving them specific acts to achieve in order to be rescued by npc's, they can start expanding their agency. <br /> If they don't manage them, Etta can manage quite a lot on her own, but I want them to figure out for themselves what t they can do to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:50:20-07:00","id":1109699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1109697#post1109697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posted the last one before it was finished - so, I want them to get to the stage where they can perform such acts, but I was thinking in this case that by giving them specific acts to achieve in order to be rescued by npc's, they can start expanding their agency.<br /> If they don't manage them, Etta can manage quite a lot on her own, but I want them to figure out for themselves what t they can do to help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand that. But you can still allow them agency. For example, you can have a Corr plan, a Spirit plan, and a mundane plan, and let them decide which one they want to go with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T05:01:36-07:00","id":1109701,"title":"","content":"True - and they'll probably choose the mundane plan so I'd better prepare for that! <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:20:50-07:00","id":1109774,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what Saikou said, even with unexperienced players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested?p=1109309#post1109309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we all work full time and Laura's player is in a long-distance relationship so we can't do daytime or weekends. So instead we meet frequently for short sessions - weekly if possible. 7-9 is what we aim for, although last time was delayed by half an hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess anything is better than nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:42:01-07:00","id":1115024,"title":"","content":"So, next session tonight, I've got some loose goals for the players to achieve in order to get away scot free but will tailor those to the time we have. Those are mentioned above. <br /> I've got an npc waiting in the wings to help with escape via correspondence, spirit or conventional means (va, ecstatic, son of ether) depending on what they choose although I can roll with it if they choose &quot;other&quot; as well. <br /> At the end of their escape they'll go to the va's mansion/chantry to have their identities scrubbed and be told to lie low for a week at Glastonbury Festival. There (in downtime) they can seek mentors to allow them to be inducted into a tradition. <br /> <br /> Some thoughts on future campaign ideas:<br /> I plan to build up their knowledge of the supernatural gradually in game;<br /> I'm going to avoid nephandi and &quot;evil&quot; for shades of grey for quite a while, to let them see the technocracy in a more rational light;<br /> In my world the reckoning took place in 2004;<br /> Most of the plot will hopefully be player-driven to begin with, not going to touch masters or the tradition council for a while until they are established in (and familiar with) their tradition. <br /> <br /> I'll post the planned plot ties for each character in the next few days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:58:23-07:00","id":1115141,"title":"","content":"Just a little warning on plans. The players will almost always find a way to nullify them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:56:02-07:00","id":1115493,"title":"","content":"Of course :-) that's why I'm keeping it vague, or thinking about themes rather than &quot;they will do this!&quot;<br /> Last night was cancelled due to illness so I've got more time to flesh out npc's which is nice. Might even get some floor plans of the facility ready as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}